  "details": "VRChat version: 2022.2-8d03df2a56 \nDescription of the bug:\nAccording to the docs of EAC, the EAC will be removed if I uninstalled the game.\nHowever, after uninstalling VRC, the service EasyAntiCheat_EOS will still be on the services list.\nPlease uninstall EAC when uninstalling VRChat  Some friend found a document *for developer* and the command in the doc, `EasyAntiCheat_EOS_Setup.exe uninstall <ProductId-in-json>`, is working for me to uninstall EAC.\nThat's why  I think the mechanism to uninstall EAC is not broken and I think this is a VRChat’s fault.\nMy environment is Windows11 so I thought that may be because of using unsupported Windows version. \nHowever, some my friends reported me that same happens on windows 10 so I reported here.\n \nSource EAC doc: https://www.easy.ac/en-us/support/game/guides/installer/\nSource EAC doc for devs: https://dev.epicgames.com/docs/services/en-US/GameServices/AntiCheat/index.html#configuration\nSteps to reproduce:\n 1) uninstall VRChat via steam\n 2) find service list on some app (e.g. Task Manager)  3) you can find EasyAntiCheat_EOS",
